clueweb09-en0006-30-06669.0 Help Put Remarkable Trees of Virginia into Virginia's public libraries! Help Put Remarkable Trees of Virginia into Virginia's public libraries! We want public libraries across Virginia to have a copy of Remarkable Trees in their collection. Thanks to a challenge grant from the Virginia 4-H Foundation and the Virginia Foundation for the Humanities we have 30 books that we can give to libraries, provided they are matched by a local gift. The concept is simple, purchase one book for a local public library, and we will send you one copy free of charge. When we reach 60 libraries, the offer ends! Libraries pledged to date: Central Baptist Academy Hampton University Museum Williamsburg Regional Library James City County Master Gardener Library Great Falls Library Sherwood Regional Library (Fairfax) Fairfax Regional Library Chesterfield Historical Society of Virginia Chesterfield County Public Library Sandston Elementary School Montgomery-Floyd Regional Library system (two copies) Pearisburg Public Library (Pearisburg) Iris Brammer Library (Narrows) Roanoke County Master Gardner
clueweb09-en0006-55-08251.0 Group Study Rooms - FCPL [Fairfax County, Virginia] [Fairfax County] Search Site: Home Living Here Doing Business Visiting Departments & Agencies [*] Group Study Rooms [*] homepage > library > about the library > library services > group study rooms [*] Home Account Services Research Tools Catalog Databases Events Library Branches Good Reading About the Library Site Index Group study rooms are only available at the Burke Centre, City of Fairfax Regional, Oakton and Sherwood Regional libraries. The rooms are for use by small groups working together on projects that require a level of interaction that might be distracting to other library users. These rooms are available at no charge for use by organizations and individuals for educational, cultural and informational community meetings and programs. They are available during regular operating hours. Reservations may be made by contacting your local library branch. Reservations are accepted on a first-come, first-served basis. Group study room rules and
