clueweb09-enwp01-18-05268.0 London Public Library - Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia London Public Library From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search The London Public Library is the public library system of London, Ontario Canada. London Public Library opened in November, 1896. It now has 16 branches open to the public. The branches are named Beacock, Byron, Carson, Central, Cherryhill, Crouch, East London, Glanworth, Jalna, Lambeth, Landon, Masonville, Northridge, Pond Mills, Sherwood, and Westmount. The Central Library, which used remodeled space that formerly housed a Bay outlet, which not only allowed for an economical expansion of the branch but also enjoyed a more central location in the city's downtown core to aid in revitalizing the area. In addition, major additional outside donations enabled the construction of the Wolf Performance Hall, a state-of-the-art concert hall which hosts music and theatre performances. The Central Library is also home to the Reading Garden which is equipped with seating and multiple water features. The
