clueweb09-en0002-04-26891.0 Human Impacts and Hazards [] [Skip to main content][Skip to navigation] Exploring the Yellowstone Geoecosystem A Digital Resource Collection for Teaching and Learning Integrating Research and Education > Yellowstone > Key Topics > Human Impacts and Hazards Human Impacts and Hazards This page was written by Denny Capps as part of the DLESE Community Services Project: Integrating Research in Education. [Thermal image of Yellowstone Fires.] [show]Show caption [hide]Hide Thermal image of Yellowstone Fires. Image courtesy of NASA Airborne Sensor Facility. Details Volcanism Resources describing the impacts and hazards associated with Yellowstone volcanics. [show]Show me information about volcanism [hide]Hide A Living, Breathing Caldera. This report describes the crustal deformation of the Yellowstone Hotspot from 1923 to 1995. Measurements show that the Yellowstone Caldera underwent rapid uplift from 1923 to 1985; this was followed by ten years of subsidence. The report also summarizes the University of Utah's research program to monitor the caldera using GPS stations.
